NOTICE
======

Iris is the desktop assistant for publik (publikhq.com) — a text-first,
menu-bar AI companion for macOS. You summon it with a global hotkey
(ctrl + option), type a question, and it answers with full context of
what's on your screen, optionally flying a small cursor to point at the
relevant UI element.

Iris is a fork of Clicky by Farza (https://github.com/farzaa/clicky),
which is licensed under the MIT License. The original MIT license text is
preserved in this directory as LICENSE.upstream, and that license continues
to apply to the portions of this codebase derived from Clicky.

Changes in this fork:
- Voice features were removed: AssemblyAI streaming transcription,
  OpenAI/Apple Speech transcription fallbacks, push-to-talk dictation,
  and ElevenLabs text-to-speech. Iris is text-first.
- Third-party analytics (PostHog) and email collection were removed.
- The app was rebranded from Clicky to Iris.

Based on Clicky by Farza (MIT).
